{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-explainer-about-tetris-how-the-game-was-made-and-some-history-of-tetris-write-like-you/audio/main-127cf0cf9ffa.mp3","durationSec":229.728,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.18,"text":"Many famous games come from big companies."},{"start":3.04,"end":3.86,"text":"Tetris is different."},{"start":4.76,"end":6.1,"text":"It started with one person."},{"start":6.76,"end":8.44,"text":"His name was Alexey Pajitnov."},{"start":9.18,"end":10.48,"text":"He was a computer engineer."},{"start":11.56,"end":13.48,"text":"In 1984 he worked in Moscow."},{"start":14.46,"end":20.4,"text":"Moscow was the capital of the Soviet Union, a very large country that lasted from 1922 to 1991."},{"start":21.4,"end":24.34,"text":"Pajitnov worked at the Dorodnitsyn Computing Centre."},{"start":24.34,"end":27.7,"text":"This was a research place under the Academy of Sciences of the Soviet Union."},{"start":28.06,"end":30.12,"text":"His main job was not games."},{"start":30.66,"end":31.72,"text":"He tested computers."},{"start":32.46,"end":34.84,"text":"But in his free time he liked puzzles."},{"start":35.76,"end":39.38,"text":"That love of puzzles was the start of Tetris."},{"start":40.82,"end":46.98,"text":"In this story, we can follow three steps: the source, the change, and the result."},{"start":47.94,"end":50.22,"text":"The source was one man and his puzzles."},{"start":51.26,"end":55.38,"text":"Pajitnov built the first Tetris on a machine called the Elektronika 60."},{"start":56.09,"end":58.32,"text":"This was a Soviet minicomputer."},{"start":58.32,"end":61.76,"text":"It was made by a company named Elektronika in the city of Voronezh."},{"start":62.48,"end":66.1,"text":"The company made this computer from 1978 to 1991."},{"start":67.06,"end":68.64,"text":"The Elektronika 60 was big."},{"start":69.24,"end":71.12,"text":"It sat in a rack, like a metal shelf."},{"start":71.62,"end":72.96,"text":"It had no built-in screen."},{"start":73.5,"end":75,"text":"It could not show pictures at all."},{"start":75.78,"end":77.58,"text":"So the first Tetris had no drawings."},{"start":78.18,"end":82.36,"text":"The falling blocks were made from text characters, like letters and symbols on a page."},{"start":82.95,"end":86.52,"text":"A block was just a group of characters that moved down the screen."},{"start":87.34,"end":89,"text":"This was a very simple look."},{"start":89.42,"end":91.5,"text":"But the idea under it was strong."},{"start":92.36,"end":93.58,"text":"The source was simple."},{"start":94.32,"end":95.56,"text":"The change came soon."},{"start":96.22,"end":98.22,"text":"The name Tetris has two parts."},{"start":98.88,"end":100.84,"text":"The first part comes from the word tetra."},{"start":101.54,"end":102.32,"text":"Tetra means four."},{"start":103.14,"end":105.84,"text":"Every Tetris piece is made of four small squares."},{"start":106.6,"end":108.36,"text":"The second part comes from tennis."},{"start":109.42,"end":111.86,"text":"Pajitnov liked tennis, so he joined the two words."},{"start":112.42,"end":114.34,"text":"Tetra plus tennis became Tetris."},{"start":114.34,"end":116.52,"text":"The game itself is easy to explain."},{"start":116.52,"end":118.36,"text":"Pieces fall from the top."},{"start":118.86,"end":120.4,"text":"The player turns them and moves them."},{"start":121.04,"end":122.64,"text":"A full line of squares disappears."},{"start":123.38,"end":124.72,"text":"The screen gets clean again."},{"start":125.7,"end":127.32,"text":"This mix is the heart of the game."},{"start":128.04,"end":128.94,"text":"The rule is small."},{"start":129.48,"end":130.2,"text":"The play is deep."},{"start":131.04,"end":134.62,"text":"Many people in Japan know this feeling from small puzzle games on a train ride."},{"start":135.56,"end":137.42,"text":"A short game fits a short trip."},{"start":138.14,"end":140.4,"text":"The idea from Moscow fits that life too."},{"start":140.96,"end":141.94,"text":"Now the change."},{"start":141.94,"end":144.26,"text":"The game did not stay in one office."},{"start":145,"end":146.3,"text":"People in Moscow liked it."},{"start":146.88,"end":148.46,"text":"They copied it and gave it to friends."},{"start":149.42,"end":151.14,"text":"Copies moved from one computer to another."},{"start":152.04,"end":153.86,"text":"Later, versions appeared on home computers."},{"start":154.9,"end":157.54,"text":"The game left the Soviet Union and reached other countries."},{"start":158.34,"end":160.12,"text":"This spread was fast for the time."},{"start":160.84,"end":162.52,"text":"It happened with no big advertising."},{"start":163.44,"end":164.8,"text":"The reason was the game itself."},{"start":165.48,"end":167.02,"text":"It was easy to learn in one minute."},{"start":167.56,"end":168.76,"text":"It was hard to stop."},{"start":169.44,"end":171.88,"text":"One copy made ten more copies."},{"start":172.32,"end":176.02,"text":"In the lens of source, change, and result, this is the change."},{"start":176.86,"end":180.7,"text":"A small puzzle from a research centre was now a game in many homes."},{"start":181.22,"end":182.6,"text":"The result was still coming."},{"start":183.3,"end":185.18,"text":"The result came with a small machine."},{"start":186.08,"end":188.44,"text":"Nintendo is a Japanese video game company."},{"start":189.28,"end":194.18,"text":"In 1989 Nintendo released a handheld console called the Game Boy."},{"start":194.86,"end":198.06,"text":"A handheld console is a game machine you hold in your hands."},{"start":198.94,"end":201.44,"text":"Nintendo also released Tetris for the Game Boy."},{"start":202.28,"end":203.46,"text":"This was the big moment."},{"start":204.1,"end":208.06,"text":"People could now play Tetris on a bus, at school, or at home."},{"start":208.82,"end":212.36,"text":"The small screen and the small game were a perfect match."},{"start":213.36,"end":216.82,"text":"Tetris on the Game Boy helped the game become huge around the world."},{"start":217.4,"end":219.62,"text":"So the story ends far from its start."},{"start":220.36,"end":223.38,"text":"The source was a text-only computer in Moscow."},{"start":224.1,"end":229.12,"text":"The result was a game in millions of pockets, made famous by a company from Japan."}],"words":[{"text":"Many","start":0,"end":0.3},{"text":"famous","start":0.3,"end":0.66},{"text":"games","start":0.66,"end":0.98},{"text":"come","start":0.98,"end":1.28},{"text":"from","start":1.28,"end":1.5},{"text":"big","start":1.5,"end":1.7},{"text":"companies","start":1.7,"end":2.18},{"text":"Tetris","start":3.04,"end":3.24},{"text":"is","start":3.24,"end":3.48},{"text":"different","start":3.48,"end":3.86},{"text":"It","start":4.76,"end":4.88},{"text":"started","start":4.88,"end":5.16},{"text":"with","start":5.16,"end":5.42},{"text":"one","start":5.42,"end":5.7},{"text":"person","start":5.7,"end":6.1},{"text":"His","start":6.76,"end":6.88},{"text":"name","start":6.88,"end":7.1},{"text":"was","start":7.1,"end":7.3},{"text":"Alexey","start":7.3,"end":7.9},{"text":"Pajitnov","start":7.9,"end":8.44},{"text":"He","start":9.18,"end":9.4},{"text":"was","start":9.4,"end":9.52},{"text":"a","start":9.52,"end":9.66},{"text":"computer","start":9.66,"end":9.96},{"text":"engineer","start":9.96,"end":10.48},{"text":"In","start":11.56,"end":11.68},{"text":"1984","start":11.68,"end":12.28},{"text":"he","start":12.52,"end":12.74},{"text":"worked","start":12.74,"end":12.94},{"text":"in","start":12.94,"end":13.14},{"text":"Moscow","start":13.14,"end":13.48},{"text":"Moscow","start":14.46,"end":14.62},{"text":"was","start":14.62,"end":14.84},{"text":"the","start":14.84,"end":15},{"text":"capital","start":15,"end":15.24},{"text":"of","start":15.24,"end":15.44},{"text":"the","start":15.44,"end":15.56},{"text":"Soviet","start":15.56,"end":15.86},{"text":"Union","start":15.86,"end":16.26},{"text":"a","start":16.64,"end":16.84},{"text":"very","start":16.84,"end":17.08},{"text":"large","start"